          "sectionId": "section:f0b08b69-540e-46a8-857d-646b02b2795b",
          "sectionRevisionId": "sectionrev:bd58eb09-3a1c-4039-82a9-ba5320cd44b3",
          "order": 0,
          "title": "Exact predicate",
          "prose": "`is_empty` returns true if `points.is_empty()` is true or `n_contours == 0` is true. If those conditions disagree, the result is still true; it is false only when `points` is nonempty and `n_contours` is nonzero. The `Outline` declaration documents `n_contours` as the number of contours and `points` as the flattened points across them. They are distinct stored fields, matching the two separate tests in the predicate.",
          "spokenText": "They are distinct stored fields, matching the two separate tests in the predicate.",
